		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Neo-Hookean model in XPBD?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=39213#p39213"><![CDATA[
Hi,<br><br>can the classical nonlinear elastic material models (like the Neo-Hookean) be used in the <a href="http://blog.mmacklin.com/2016/09/15/xpbd/" class="postlink">XPBD</a> framework?<br>In the paper they only use the simple St. Venant Kirchhoff elastic model.<br>Is the simulation going to remain stable while simulating using more complicated models under high time-steps (e.g. 1/20 s)?<br><br>(I consider a 3D tetrahedral model as a simulation object.)<br><br>Thanks.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=12146">GeorgeJennings</a> — Thu Apr 20, 2017 11:47 pm</p><hr />
